WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
These giants move slowly.

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.060
Let's make 60 years visible.

3
00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:10.317
In 1619, Johannes Kepler linked a planet's distance

4
00:00:10.257 --> 00:00:12.797
from the Sun to the time it takes to orbit.

5
00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:16.347
Jupiter takes almost 12 Earth years to circle

6
00:00:16.287 --> 00:00:16.847
the Sun.

7
00:00:18.427 --> 00:00:20.447
Saturn takes about 29 and a half.

8
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:25.213
Mark both positions at the same moment, connect

9
00:00:25.153 --> 00:00:28.233
them, and repeat at equal time steps.

10
00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:32.745
Speed up 60 years, watch the relationship unfold.

11
00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:36.408
These lines are our drawing, not strings in space.

12
00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:40.982
Beautiful to look at, fun to draw, and a way to

13
00:00:40.922 --> 00:00:42.562
understand how a system works.

14
00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:44.182
Try drawing it together.
